The fold `(f<A>(a), ...)' and the call `g(f<A>(a)...)' in a member
function template expand both the function parameter pack and the template
parameter pack per element ([temp.variadic]/9).  In the fold the template
pack kept its first element in every instance, and the body of a constexpr
member was converted without expanding `a'.
